tle or no background in the study of China.", "catalogBreadth": "(GHB)", "catalogDistr": "(CA-AS, HST-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "This crosslisted class is one of several topical courses in the Department of Asian Studies at the 2000-level that offer introductions to Chinese civilization (CAPS 2230, CAPS 2231,\u00a0CAPS 2232). Students may take more than one of these introductory courses for credit.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2839, "crseId": 372854, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "CAPS", "catalogNbr": "2435", "titleShort": "Global Maoism", "titleLong": "Global Maoism: History and Present", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 17754, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "02:45PM", "timeEnd": "04:00PM", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/09/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "ps786", "firstName": "Peidong", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Sun"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Goldwin Smith Hall 348", "bldgDescr": "Goldwin Smith Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "GSH348", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/20/2023", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "HIST", "catalogNbr": "2435", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/23/2023", "sessionEndDt": "05/20/2023", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "Maoism and Chinese Communism are not history after Mao's death in 1976. In China, Maoism holds the key to the enduring success of the Chinese Communist Party (CCP), one of the most remarkable organizations of the 20th and 21st centuries that has survived the collapse of communism in Europe and the USSR. With the beneficial transformation brought by capitalism and globalization in China, the end of the Cold War and the narrative of the \"end of history\" cannot explain the resurgence of Maoism.", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "(ALC-AS, HA-AS, HST-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2839, "crseId": 372857, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "CAPS", "catalogNbr": "2575", "titleShort": "Tyranny&Dignity: Chinese Women", "titleLong": "Tyranny and Dignity: Chinese Women from the Cultural Revolution to the White Paper Revolution", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 17755, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "01:00PM", "timeEnd": "02:15PM", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/09/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "ps786", "firstName": "Peidong", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Sun"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Rockefeller Hall 230", "bldgDescr": "Rockefeller Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "RCK230", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Time spent outside of the classroom viewing Chinese independent documentary films, music, and photographs; and additional workshops with film directors, singers, and photographers will be required."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/20/2023", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "FGSS", "catalogNbr": "2575", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "HIST", "catalogNbr": "2575", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/23/2023", "sessionEndDt": "05/20/2023", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This course focuses on the human condition of Chinese women after 1949. In the name of the Women's liberation movement since the early 1900s, do Chinese women eventually hold up the half sky? From the cradle to the grave, what was most challenging in women's life? How did political, economic, and cultural forces frame women's professional careers and private life? No judgments nor imaginations. Using multi-media, such as Chinese independent documentary films, music, and photographs, students will discover the hidden stories behind the mainstream narratives. Workshops with film directors, pop music singers, and photographers offer students an unusual way of accessing all backstage field experiences.", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "(ALC-AS, HA-AS, HST-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2839, "crseId": 372230, "crseOfferNbr": 3, "subject": "CAPS", "catalogNbr": "2932", "titleShort": "Engendering China", "titleLong": "Engendering China", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 7243, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "09:40AM", "timeEnd": "10:55AM", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/09/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "yd367", "firstName": "Yue", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Du"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Hollister Hall 206", "bldgDescr": "Hollister Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "HLS206", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/23/2023", "endDt": "05/20/2023", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "ASIAN", "catalogNbr": "2291", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "FGSS", "catalogNbr": "2932", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "HIST", "catalogNbr": "2932", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/23/2023", "sessionEndDt": "05/20/2023", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "In contemporary China, as in many other places of the world, the ideology and social reality of gender relations is highly paradoxical. Women are flattered for their power as consumers and commitment to the family while they are also expected to engage in wage-earning employment. Men, on the other hand, face constant pressure of being tough and social problems such as costly betrothal gifts as unintended consequences of a gender regime that is supposedly male-oriented. Are these paradoxes a betrayal of the socialist experiment of erasing gender differences? Are they remnants of China's long imperial tradition? This course explores the power dynamics of gender relations in China from ancient times to the present. It leads students to examine scholarship that challenges the popularly accepted myth of lineal progression of China toward gender equality, and to understand women's and men's life choices in various historical settings. At the same time, this course guides students to adopt \"gender\" as a useful analytical category, treating China as a case study through which students are trained to \"engender\" any society past and present.", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "(HA-AS, HST-AS, SCD-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "